  "id": "Compound::DB00652 - Gene::4988",
  "verbalization": "Pentazocine is linked to Oprm1 through a series of molecular and pharmacological relationships that collectively support its interaction with the opioid receptor. The evidence suggests that Pentazocine, as part of the Organonitrogen Compound class, binds to Oprm1, with some evidence pointing to its classification as both a Competitive Opioid Antagonist and a Partial Opioid Agonist. This dual classification implies that Pentazocine may exhibit complex receptor interactions, potentially modulating Oprm1 activity in a context-dependent manner. The shared lowest common ancestors with Butorphanol and Levallorphan further highlight the structural and functional similarities among these compounds, reinforcing their potential to interact with opioid receptors. The integration of these pathways suggests that Pentazocine may act as a modulator of Oprm1, possibly through a mechanism involving receptor activation or antagonism, depending on the specific context of its use. The evidence from the dataset supports a role for Pentazocine in influencing Oprm1 function, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
